# Cursor workflow

Product memory is `CLAUDE.md`. Do not copy it into rules or `AGENTS.md`.

- This checkout is shared. Owen pushes to `origin/main`. `git fetch origin` before starting feature work.
- Never `git add -A` or `git add .`. Stage explicit paths only. `.env` and `ledger/*.csv` are secrets.
- Untracked files you did not create are someone else's WIP. Leave them.
- New work goes on a branch, not on `main`.
- After pushing a feature branch, open a PR against `main` in the same turn. Don't wait to be asked. Skip only if a PR for that branch already exists. Don't merge unless asked.
- GitHub CLI is a portable (no-admin) copy at `%LOCALAPPDATA%\gh-portable\bin\gh.exe`, same pattern as Node. Always invoke that path (do not assume `gh` is on PATH). If `gh auth status` is not logged in, run `gh auth login --hostname github.com --git-protocol https --web --skip-ssh-key` and give Jacob the one-time code; do not fall back to a compare URL until that login has actually failed. GitHub MCP is read-only for PRs on this machine — do not use it to create pull requests.
- Node is a portable (no-admin) copy. Integrated terminals prepend `%LOCALAPPDATA%\node-portable\node-v24.16.0-win-x64` via `.vscode/settings.json`. If `node` is missing, that folder is not installed yet — do not assume a system Node.
